      "input_bands": "contiguous band0..bandN in declared order",
      "output_bands": "row-major matrix0..matrixN",
      "constants": "Finite lowercase binary64 hex; raw integer admission remains +/-2^53"
    },
    "numeric": "Scaled fixed Commons Math3.6.1 SVD with library getRank cutoff, compensated pseudoinverse assembly and (V/sigma)*U ordering. Exact binary64 BigDecimal products against original RHS avoid small-signal loss from B normalization. Exact nonzero constant-column RHS centering and combined anchor restoration only at full column rank. Zero-rank solve/pseudoinverse return zeros.",
    "mask": "Any input NoData, numerical-singular inverse or nonfinite Float64 kernel output masks the entire matrix; valid source Infinity rejects, including masked peers. Actual keys/time metadata retained; no invented empty/global grid.",
    "grid_and_bridge": "Fresh common-grid/single-item asset proof and matching time dimensions before merges. Shared bounded dry-run trace admission retains origins without treating stale upstream band labels as actual input order. Actual Python cube and native provider enforce ordered bands; every native tile must match metadata dimensions before its admitted budget is used.",
    "source_free": "Finite inverse/pseudoinverse can fold with normalized local rank policy and actual cast stages, without inventing a raster grid. Source-free masked/singular/nonfinite inverse or final Float32 overflow rejects; source-free rank-deficient solve still rejects.",
